Shared Library AWS Deployment and CI_CD Automation Plan
🧭 Overview
The meeting aligned the deployment of the shared library through two CloudFormation scopes: account bootstrap, executed once per AWS account, and environment deployment, executed once per environment. The team agreed to replace manual procedures with an automated IAC and MDTC v2 pipeline covering bootstrap, environment configuration, secret handling, CI packaging, Docker image publication to ECR, and application deployment. Key dependencies remain the selection of a clean deployment account, final repository ownership, Artifactory rotation validation, Ping environment and promotion rules, required network values, and platform gateway details.
Account bootstrap will create the CA S3 location, use the static Central CA KMS key, configure registry access in Secrets Manager, establish required roles and tags, and be validated from a clean account.
Each environment will use a customized configuration file and an Artifactory-based deployment pipeline, with CI scans, .zip packaging, artifact publication, and environment-specific CloudFormation parameters.
Ping integration will use SAML for the UI and JWT for Jobs API access; Admin role and Viewer role entitlements must be created and mapped to application groups.
Repository access, IAC pipeline ownership, VPC values, the correct non-production Ping endpoint, secret-rotation behavior, and platform gateway tenant details require follow-up.
