3. Environment Deployment Pipeline and Configuration
Background:
Environment deployment is separate from account bootstrap and requires environment-specific CloudFormation parameters. The reviewed pipeline was tested in the MSA account, while the current example and documentation still use S3 mode and contain obsolete script references.
Key Conclusion/Resolution:
The environment deployment pipeline is the second CloudFormation stage and runs once per environment. It requires the template name, stack name, VPC ID, private subnet, CodeBuild security group, Lambda subnet ID, S3 VPC endpoint, and private API Gateway endpoint ID.
The pipeline will move from S3 mode to Artifactory mode. CI will clone the repository, run scans, create the required .zip, and publish it to Artifactory; Artifactory mode allows a deployer to select the release version, whereas S3 mode relies on S3 versioning. The pipeline configuration key must reference the target environment file rather than the example test.yaml.
Each environment must use a copied and renamed .yaml file. The file contains the bootstrap role ARN, application-owner and ABAC tags, application ID, Job ID, Job API, network values, API Gateway settings, secrets, logging, source and README URLs, feature flags, and entitlement mappings. The application ID illustrated as RX7742 must be replaced with the deployment-specific value; separate TPI app IDs may be used for isolation.
