4. Network, Ping Authentication, and Entitlement Mapping
Background:
The application requires private network connectivity to Ping and separate authentication paths for UI users and programmatic consumers. Ping-side objects cannot be completed until the deployment configuration and request details are available.
Key Conclusion/Resolution:
The application must run in a private, routable subnet so it can communicate with Ping. The environment requires the VPC ID, private subnet IDs, Lambda subnet ID, CodeBuild security group, standard S3 VPC endpoint, and private API Gateway endpoint ID. The configured space name is beta; the Job API configuration is used by downstream systems and does not require a functional change.
The UI and front end will use SAML. Programmatic and automated Jobs API access will use JWT. The initial Ping metadata value is only a placeholder because the metadata endpoint is not exposed. After Ping configuration, the Ping team will provide the SAML metadata file for upload to Cognito.
For multifamily, the baseline entitlements are Admin role for configuration and Viewer role for document visibility without configuration access. If the application uses four roles, four corresponding entitlements are required. Ping groups must map directly to the application entitlements and application roles, and the same entitlement mapping is used by JWT configuration.
