5. Platform Gateway, Runtime Features, and Resilience
Background:
The application includes platform gateway settings and optional runtime features that affect Bedrock access, completion processing, logging, and operational resilience.
Key Conclusion/Resolution:
Bedrock calls will use the platform gateway, which requires a tenant ID and URL. The circuit breaker remains enabled so repeated Bedrock failures do not cause continuous calls and normal processing can resume when Bedrock becomes available.
The completion hook remains enabled and invokes a Lambda function that writes a log. The earlier MQ approach was not implemented because the MQ integration did not work; polling is used instead. The document knowledge base and MCP features remain disabled because of cost and security considerations. CloudWatch is used for logs, with info configured as the current log level and debug considered for Rob’s initial troubleshooting.
